sequenceDiagram
  participant A as Host A / current writer
  participant M as Shared memory
  participant F as Artifacts / receipts
  participant B as Host B / receiver
  A->>M: Read context + newest node + revision N
  A->>F: Execute and retain real output
  A->>M: Persist node, next action, artifact identities
  A->>M: Recheck N, transfer writer, commit N+1
  A->>M: Read back committed state
  B->>M: Resolve same root, read N+1
  B->>F: Check existing artifacts and source hashes
  alt Changed evidence or revision
    B->>M: Preserve discrepancy, reconcile before writing
  else Current evidence and ownership
    B->>M: Read relevant experience and preparation
    B->>F: Perform review variation and retain receipts
    B->>M: Commit review and next action as N+2
  end
  A->>M: Late message arrives, read current revision
  Note over A,B: Old writer skips duplicate work, paths alone do not prove shared memory
  Note over M,F: Actual Agent turns are separate evidence from test-process handoffs
